com/barrie-diy-do-it-yourself-meetup-group/events/316736754/","description":"Camping at Lake Charles\nA getaway with the full camping vibe — lake views, BBQ, bonfires, kayaking, nature walks and stargazing — but with everyone staying in their own rustic cabin.\n\nWe’ll spend the day relaxing and exploring, then gather around the fire at night for food, drinks, music and good conversation. 🔥💕\n\nPlease note: this is an off-grid experience with limited electricity, no Wi-Fi or drinking water provided, shared washroom facilities, and guests should bring their own bedding and essentials.\n\nCome solo, meet new people, and enjoy a little escape from the city. 💗\n\nPlease DM to reserve a spot. We can car pool as well from longbranch go/Kipling station.\n\nEach Cabin cost $80, 2 person max. ( will share the link to book)","startDate":"2026-10-10T11:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"195 N Queen St, Etobicoke, ON M9C 4Y1","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Etobicoke","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"195 N Queen St, Etobicoke, ON M9C 4Y1, Etobicoke, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Social Circle ✨","url":"https://www.meetup.com/barrie-diy-do-it-yourself-meetup-group/"},"performer":"The Social Circle ✨"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Beautiful Rouge National Urban Park","url":"https://www.meetup.com/forest-footprints/events/312650453/","description":"This classic Rouge Valley hike features excellent examples of rare Carolinian ecosystems while traversing a 200-year-old former logging route where pine trees were cut and floated down the river, eventually bound for ship building yards in Europe.\nThis is an intermediate hike.\nWe will be parking at Rouge National Urban Park, Twyn Rivers Day Use Area. 55 Twyn Rivers Dr, Scarborough, ON M1B 5R9\nIf you get lost, please call my cell: 647-949-6912\n\n**Important Reminder:**\nBy participating in this hike, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to the Liability Waiver and Acknowledgement of Risk. If you have not done so, we kindly request that you refrain from participating in this event. We appreciate your cooperation and look forward to an enjoyable and safe adventure!\n• Arrive on time! Please be punctual, as the group will leave on time.\n• Know your limits! Choose the hike that match your fitness level.","startDate":"2026-10-10T12:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Twyn Rivers Parking Lot","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"55 Twyn Rivers Drive, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Forest Footprints","url":"https://www.meetup.com/forest-footprints/"},"performer":"Forest Footprints"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Community Wim Hof practice","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/events/316635624/","description":"It's better when we're together. Come and experience the power of the WHM with a wonderful group of people. We breathe, we go into the cold and we teach our bodies to heat up properly. We develop resilience and the mindset to use these powerful healing tools over and over again, all year round. This gathering is fully guided by Wim Hof instructor Steve Beattie.\n\nIf you are new to this, come on down, enjoy the support and practice in a safe way with us. If you already have a WHM practice this meetup is a great way to take it to the next level, and make lots of new friends.\n\nThere will be a fire, snacks and drinks shared by other attendees. We have been doing this 6 for years!\n\n**What to bring?**\n\n* Yoga mat\n* Weather-appropriate clothing (better to dress too warm!)\n* Bathing suite, towel\n* Water shoes (optional)\n\nIn extreme weather being prepared is very important. Especially if it's your first time, please read up on how to come prepared [here.](https://www.breathinginnature.com/wim-hof-method-meetup/)\n\nLearn more about our Wim Hof meetups, workshops, breath classes, wilderness trips, medicine work and special events at **[Breathing in Nature](https://breathinginnature.com/)**.\n\nJoin the \"**[Wim Hof Toronto](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1714218015474146/)**\" group on Facebook to see all of our local events.\n\nThis is a free event made possible by our Gift Economy. You can learn more about the Gift Economy [here](https://breathinginnature.com/gift-economy/).","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Humber Bay Park-West","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Humber Bay Park Road W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wim Hof Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Wim Hof Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Drop-In Pickleball – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316635436/","description":"🏓 **Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\nRSVP on Meetup does *not* guarantee your spot.\nTo play, you must register and pay in advance through our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=xYXBXd6)**\n📞 Or call: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\n**Limited to 18 players.** Once full, no additional players will be admitted.\n\n***\n\n**Beginner Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\n\nNew to pickleball? We’ve got the perfect session for you!\nJoin us for **Beginner Drop-In Pickleball** at the Miles Nadal JCC — a welcoming and supportive environment for those just getting started with the game. Whether you're still learning the rules or building confidence on the court, this is a great opportunity to play, practice, and meet fellow beginners.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Please check in with security and stop by the front desk upon arrival.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **What to Expect:**\n\n* Designed for **beginner-level players** with some familiarity with the rules and scoring\n* Equipment available: borrow paddles and balls with a $20 cash deposit + valid ID\n* Friendly rotations so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Supportive and inclusive environment — no pressure, just fun and learning!\n\n***\n\nCome ready to move, meet new people, and improve your game one rally at a time. We look forward to seeing you on the court!","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Saturday Beach Volleyball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/brampton-volleyball-meetup-group/events/316635787/","description":"**NO SHOWS are STRICTLY NOT ALLOWED as it impacts the game so please respect your RSVPs**\n\nWelcome to **Season 4 of Outdoor Volleyball**\n\nWednesday Evening (Mahaffy Park - Grass Court)\nSaturday Morning (Chinguacousy Park - Sand Court)\n\n**FEES: Your first volleyball game with the group is FREE! Come check out the group, meet the players, and see if it’s a good fit for you.**\n\n**To confirm you spot, E-Transfer** to mech.swapnil@gmail.com.\n\n**2026 Remaining Season Fees per player- $20 (Aug to October)**\n**Drop-in Fee per player - $5 per day**\n\n**If payment is not received, you will be put on the waitlist.**","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chinguacousy Park Brampton","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Brampton","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Donald M. Gordon Chinguacousy Park, 9050 Bramalea Rd, Brampton, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Brampton Volleyball and Social Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/brampton-volleyball-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Brampton Volleyball and Social Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"All-Level &Beginner Friendly $10 Drop In Saturday Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332798/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FRC Toronto :: Saturday Run","url":"https://www.meetup.com/founders-running-club-toronto/events/316635812/","description":"**Founders Running Club** (FRC) brings founders, investors, tech, creative people and startup enthusiasts together for weekly easy runs and networking. We like to be comfortable when we run and finish with coffee and conversations. Choose your pace or follow a pacer—pets, friends, family, are welcome.\n\n🗓️ Launched in San Francisco, July 16, 2022\n🌍 Now in 35+ cities\n📅 Running + Networking events + Community\n\n**Join the community** https://bit.ly/frc-toronto-chat\n\n**Stay updated**:\nInstagram [http://instagram.com/foundersrc/](http://instagram.com/foundersrc/)\nPodcast [http://podcast.foundersrc.com/](http://podcast.foundersrc.com/)\nLinkedIn [http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/](http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/)\nStrava [http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC](http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC)\nWebsite [http://foundersrc.com/](http://foundersrc.com/)","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"65 Front St W","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"65 Front St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Founders Running Club :: Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/founders-running-club-toronto/"},"performer":"Founders Running Club :: Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Venture Walk #024 (High Park)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-business-startups/events/316635863/","description":"**Register here:** https://luma.com/Theventurewalk\n\n🌍 Walk. Talk. Build.\n\nThe Venture Walk is a curated walk for high profile founders, operators, and investors who are actively building and backing meaningful ventures.\n\nWe meet in Toronto to walk, connect, and have real conversations about what we are creating right now. No panels. No pitches. Just ambitious minds in motion.\n\nA limited number of spots are reserved for exceptional students seeking proximity to experienced builders.\n\n☕ Format: 60 to 90 minute walk and coffee\n\n📩 Please tell us what you are building or investing in when you apply\n\n🐶 Dogs are welcome to walk with us\n\n🥾 Hiking shoes recommended, especially after rain\n\n✅ Details shared upon acceptance","startDate":"2026-10-10T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hannah's Cafe and Bakery","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1822 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M6P 3K6, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"🔥Toronto Businesses & Startups","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-business-startups/"},"performer":"🔥Toronto Businesses & Startups"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Wizards & Workouts - FREE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/events/316670375/","description":"Do you consider rolling dice strength training?\nCan you run a D&D campaign, but not a city block?\nIf so, **WIZARDS & WORKOUTS** is for you.\n\nMy name is Peter Reynolds. I'm a writer and lover of role playing games. I'm also out of shape. I've been looking for ways to motivate myself to start working out with the same enthusiasm I bring to my Dungeons & Dragons campaign.\n\nThe plan is simple: host a fun, live role playing game where players take on the role of their favourite fantasy characters. The catch? You need to exercise if you want to succeed. Fighting a dragon? A fireball might cost you 5 pushups. Crossing a rooftop? Can you balance on one foot for a minute?\n\nBy combining simple, low impact exercises, including walking & stretching, with an interactive adventure, we'll all get healthier, have fun and maybe meet some new friends along the way. All fitness levels are welcome (as are dogs), and no previous knowledge of Dungeons & Dragons is necessary.\n\nWe meet in front of Broadview subway station at 10:00 am sharp and then walk to the Outdoor Fitness Station in Riverdale Park East (there are washrooms). At noon we start walking west, through the park, ending at the Blake House Restaurant \\* (Wellesley & Jarvis) by 12:30.\n\nAll sessions are free and I’ll be running them till it gets too cold. Hope to see you there!\n\n* The Blake House is where our Sci-Fi and Fantasy Writers' Group meets every Saturday from 1pm - 4pm to critique each other’s work. For more information on this event. Check out our Meetup events page.","startDate":"2026-10-10T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Broadview Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Ontario","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"769 Broadview Avenue, Ontario, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sauble Falls Camping","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/events/314087929/","description":"Come join us for a 3-day camping getaway at Sauble Falls Provincial Park. This meetup is for anyone who wants a fun, relaxed outdoor weekend with a little adventure and a little fresh-air therapy.\nPlan for the weekend:\nSaturday: Arrive, set up camp, and enjoy kayaking/canoeing\nSunday: Hiking day and time to explore the falls and trails\nMonday: Slow morning, pack up, and head home\nImportant details:\nElectric campsites\nEveryone brings their own food, drinks, and camping gear\nGreat for people who enjoy camping, nature, and easygoing group vibes\nWater activities and hiking are part of the plan, so bring clothes and shoes for both\nWhat to bring:\nTent or camping setup\nSleeping bag and pillow\nFood and snacks for the weekend\nWater bottle\nWarm clothes for the evening\nHiking shoes\nClothes for kayaking/canoeing\nFlashlight or lantern\nToiletries and personal items","startDate":"2026-10-10T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Sauble Falls Provincial Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Wiarton","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"R.R. 3, Wiarton, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Move With Intention","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Move With Intention"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Kundalini Yoga + 5-element chimes sound bath","url":"https://www.meetup.com/yogainnatureto/events/316635984/","description":"Class description: Gentle outdoor yoga + 5-element chime meditation (attune, align, release). All levels welcome. Bring a mat and water. By donation.\n\nFind us by the tennis courts.\n\nShort bio:\n\nSinique is the founder of Yakuna Path, a somatic wellness practice that guides you back into relationship with your body and the natural world. She weaves breath, movement, sound, and elemental wisdom into every session. Her outdoor classes blend gentle yoga with a short 10-15 minute-element chime meditation — a simple way to attune, align, and release. Exp